f94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=11x+7y+14$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=11x+7y+14$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/67daa328cc6ae4cb37be386c327fb4548844fad2adc10476bdf1147c5a5d4218.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/6e58954fccd74eaf67c95df818c4c9050c35b324c5fffe4902a366cb295b8845.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j})=11{x}_{i}+7{y}_{j}+14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(11{x}_{i}+7{y}_{j}+14)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $11{x}_{i}+7{y}_{j}+14.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/state.json" "file_sha256" "06c0ee19ab86b5aed06adc4228a7233ec9d5a0640b4cc5c65c00930a8c8969de"} {"question" "q-75332" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "18eb505175667323fde6f9af69c08706940547b7d0442dc38309563563f6e641"} {"question" "q-75332" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/state.json" "file_sha256" "06c0ee19ab86b5aed06adc4228